      <section class="lr-section lr-story" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-title">
        <div class="lr-section-head">
          <span class="lr-section-number">00</span>
          <div>
            <p class="lr-eyebrow">The short version</p>
            <h2 id="story-title">A neighborhood built in chapters.</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lr-story-grid">
          <div class="lr-story-lede">
            <p class="lr-display-copy">The best-supported story is not a single founding date. It is a sequence of plans, pauses, builders, and neighbors who kept returning to the lake.</p>
            <p>Westminster Park was a named residential project by 1917. Westminster Ridge then grew on estate and woodland land in the 1920s, stalled during the Depression, and was rebuilt in a concentrated burst under architect-builder Lee Perry in 1938–39.</p>
            <a class="lr-inline-link" href="#timeline">Follow the sequence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="lr-stat-grid" aria-label="Key facts">
            <article class="lr-stat-card lr-stat-card-teal"><strong>52</strong><span>homes in the 1917 Westminster Park plan</span></article>
            <article class="lr-stat-card lr-stat-card-brick"><strong>41</strong><span>homes built or under construction by September 1938</span></article>
            <article class="lr-stat-card lr-stat-card-gold"><strong>$2</strong><span>monthly dues described for the early lake club</span></article>
            <article class="lr-stat-card lr-stat-card-ink"><strong>1</strong><span>shared lake that still organizes the neighborhood</span></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

