      <section class="lr-section lr-estate-section" id="estate" aria-labelledby="estate-title">
        <div class="lr-section-head">
          <span class="lr-section-number">03</span>
          <div>
            <p class="lr-eyebrow">The most interesting open question</p>
            <h2 id="estate-title">The house that may have started it all.</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="lr-section-note">20 Stafford Place is a strong lead, not a proven identification.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lr-estate-grid">
          <figure class="lr-estate-image">
            <img src="/public/lakenridge/images/20-stafford-map-lead.jpg" alt="1910 map with an approximate marker for 20 Stafford Place" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption><span>Research lead only</span> Approximate 20 Stafford Place location overlaid on a 1910 map. The red marker is interpretive, not a source label.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="lr-estate-copy">
            <span class="lr-lead-tag">Possible original estate house</span>
            <h3>20 Stafford Place</h3>
            <p>The 1939 <em>Architectural Forum</em> says the old estate house still stood when the subdivision was revived. Public property records describe 20 Stafford Place as a 1907 Colonial of roughly 4,012 square feet on 0.74 acres. Local street history says Stafford Place was renamed in 1934 to honor Fred P. Stafford.</p>
            <p>Its age, scale, and location make it the neighborhood’s most compelling surviving candidate. The record still needs a deed chain, historic tax card, period directory entry, or photograph that links the house to the original estate.</p>
            <details class="lr-details">
              <summary>What would confirm it?</summary>
              <p>Look for the original subdivision plat, a pre-1939 deed naming the estate, White Plains tax cards, city directories, and photographs or newspaper listings that describe the house before or during the Stafford build-out.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

