        </div>
        <div class="lr-house-explorer">
          <figure class="lr-house-image">
            <img src="/public/lakenridge/images/1938-house-types.jpg" alt="Period photographs and floor plans of Westminster Ridge house types" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>American Builder, November 1938. The models were marketed as The Lee, The Westminster, and The Greenfield.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="lr-house-panel">
            <div class="lr-house-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="1938 house types">
              <button class="lr-house-tab is-active" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-house="lee">The Lee</button>
              <button class="lr-house-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-house="westminster">The Westminster</button>
              <button class="lr-house-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-house="greenfield">The Greenfield</button>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-house-copy is-active" data-house-copy="lee"><span class="lr-house-type">01 / compact colonial</span><h3>Built for fine exposure.</h3><p>The Lee was promoted with ample rooms, a downstairs lavatory, and generous closets. It was compact, but the marketing gave it a confident architectural identity.</p></div>
            <div class="lr-house-copy" data-house-copy="westminster"><span class="lr-house-type">02 / hillside adaptation</span><h3>Made for the rolling site.</h3><p>The Westminster was designed for wooded hillsides, with automatic gas heat and a plan that could adjust to individual lots.</p></div>
            <div class="lr-house-copy" data-house-copy="greenfield"><span class="lr-house-type">03 / five-room model</span><h3>A small house with a full life.</h3><p>The Greenfield paired asbestos-cement shingles with a living room, dining alcove, equipped kitchen, and attached garage.</p></div>
            <div class="lr-house-fact"><strong>$5,800–$8,500</strong><span>reported 1938 price range</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
